pleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.7.1.stable\n- using godot_openxr_vendors plugin [5.1.0-stable](https://github.com/GodotVR/godot_openxr_vendors/releases/tag/5.1.0-stable)\n- Android build templates from official Release mirror for 4.7.1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 deploying to Quest 3\nQuest 3 v2.7 Build 5243367.360.520\n\n### Issue description\n\nI want to use the new subsampled vulkan images advertised in the 4.7 release notes, but when using the new Project setting in xr/openxr/foveation_with_subsampled_images in combination with xr/openxr/foveation_level high it does not render correctly when exported to the Quest 3. it works well when run on desktop, or when subsampled images is disabled\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- set up a new project with the current openxr vendors plugin, and enable highest foveation level, or use the MRP linked below\n- install the android build templates\n- deploy to quest 3\nthe project runs well as expected:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81197c4b-17cd-41e1-a24d-47693cfcb0a5\n\n- enable Project setting xr/openxr/foveation_with_subsampled_images\nthe project does not render correctly when deployed:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d9a5b73-270f-4e34-a365-27bdfd57ae4c\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tp-up/godot-vr-subsampling-bugreport](https://github.com/tp-up/godot-vr-subsampling-bugreport)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gist